      "issues": [
        "- The text states \"Lok Sabha — maximum strength 552 (as originally fixed; currently 543 elected seats after Anglo-Indian nomination was abolished by the 104th Amendment, 2020).\" The maximum strength after the 104th Amendment is 550 (530 from states + 20 from UTs), not 552. → The maximum strength of Lok Sabha is now 550; the 104th Amendment removed the two nominated Anglo-Indian seats, reducing the total from 552 to 550.",
        "- In the Linguistic Bridge table, \"परमादेश\" is mapped to \"Writ (e.g., बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण = Habeas Corpus)\". \"परमादेश\" is the Hindi term for Mandamus, not the generic term for writ; the generic term is \"रिट\" or \"प्रादेश\". → \"परमादेश\" should map to \"Mandamus\"; the generic term for writ is \"रिट\" or \"प्रादेश\"."
      ],
