    "sources:Content_en.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "62f9681bb51f5cd189a87440caa529ac631c5757ffb4b6762fd6ff2b043d367e",
      "kind": "sources",
      "status": "needs_reference",
      "issues": [
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: - In **Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973)**, the Supreme Court held the Preamble is **part of the Constitution** — and laid down the **Basic Structure doctrine**: Parliament can amend anything *except* the basic structure.",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: **Fundamental Duties** — Article 51A, Part IVA, added by the **42nd Amendment (1976)** on the Swaran Singh Committee's recommendation; originally 10, now **11** (the 11th — education of one's child — added by the 86th Amendment, 2002). They are **non-justiciable**.",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: - The **106th Amendment (2023)** — the *Nari Shakti Vandan Adhiniyam* — reserves one-third of seats for women in the Lok Sabha and State Assemblies, to take effect after the next delimitation and census. Connect it with Article 330A/332A.",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: Questions swap **26 November 1949** (adoption) with **26 January 1950** (enforcement), or Sachchidananda Sinha (temporary president) with Dr. Rajendra Prasad (permanent president). Always ask: *adopted or enforced? temporary or permanent?*",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: *\"Which of the following is NOT a constitutional body?\"* — options: Election Commission, Finance Commission, NITI Aayog, UPSC. Students who skim miss the \"NOT\" and pick the first familiar name. NITI Aayog (executive resolution, 2015) is the answer. Underline every NOT/EXCEPT in the question paper."
      ],
